# The specialized version of a loop reads its array through the storage that was read in the preheader.
# No program can give such an iteration a stale storage, because the iteration exits to the generic version at every operation that could move the storage.
# Fault injection, testing=MisplaceHoistedArrayStorage: the emitter offsets every hoisted storage by one word, so each read finds its neighbor's element.
# With --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime), the emitter checks the storage against a fresh read from the array in every iteration.
# If they differ, the process crashes with a named error.
# The array is filled by push, so that there is spare capacity after its last element. The fault alone reads a hole there and no memory that does not belong to the array.
